cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this software and the accompanying manuscript; cite the field-source publications when using the processed field data."
type: software
title: "CO2 plume reproducibility: injection, shut-in, and seismic footprint fits"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-28
authors:
  - family-names: Alonso-Marroquín
    given-names: Fernando
  - family-names: Tantardini
    given-names: Christian
abstract: >-
  Python scripts and data for reproducing finite-thickness CO2 plume profiles,
  injection and shut-in histories, seismic equivalent-radius fits, and numerical
  verification. The repository preserves the supplied processed field data
  and documents a source chronology query for the first Aquistore survey.
keywords:
  - carbon dioxide storage
  - porous media
  - nonlinear Fokker-Planck equation
  - porous-medium equation
  - finite-volume method
  - reproducible research
